When performing rescue breathing, avoid giving the casualty more than two rescue breaths before returning to chest compressions. Ensure the airway is clear by tilting the head back and lifting the chin before administering breaths. Continuous effective ventilation is crucial, so maintain a rhythm of 1 breath every 6 seconds when an advanced airway is in place.
