As a lone rescuer performing infant CPR, first ensure the infant's airway is open by tilting their head and lifting their chin. Give 5 initial rescue breaths to make the chest rise visibly. Then, if breaths are ineffective, alternate between 30 chest compressions (at a depth of about 1 1/2 inches using two fingers) at a rate of 100 compressions per minute, and two rescue breaths. Continue this cycle for about 1 minute before leaving to call for professional help if not alone.
